# Company Information Integration Rules

## Purpose and Scope

This rule enforces centralized business information management by requiring all business data to be sourced from a single configuration file (`businessInfo.ts`). It ensures data consistency, maintainability, and prevents hardcoded business details throughout the application.

## Standards and Requirements

### Central Data Management - STRICTLY ENFORCE
- Import and use structured data from `businessInfo.ts`
- Update business information ONLY in the central configuration file
- NEVER hardcode business details in components

### Required Import Pattern
```typescript
// ALWAYS import from businessInfo.ts
import { businessInfo, generateSEOData, getCurrentBusinessStatus, getGoogleMapsUrl } from '@data/businessInfo';

// NEVER hardcode business details
const businessName = "My Business"; // ❌ WRONG
const businessName = businessInfo.name; // ✅ CORRECT
```

### Data Consistency Rules - MANDATORY
- **Phone Display**: ALWAYS use `businessInfo.contact.phone.formatted`
- **Phone Links**: ALWAYS use `businessInfo.contact.phone.link` for tel: links
- **Address**: ALWAYS use `businessInfo.address.full` for complete address
- **Business Name**: Use `businessInfo.name` for full name, `businessInfo.shortName` for abbreviated
- **Coordinates**: Use `businessInfo.address.coordinates` for map positioning
- **Website URLs**: Use `businessInfo.website.baseUrl` for absolute URLs

### Business Information Usage
```typescript
// Contact information
businessInfo.contact.phone.formatted  // Display phone number
businessInfo.contact.phone.link       // Tel: link for calls
businessInfo.contact.email           // Email address

// Address information
businessInfo.address.full            // Complete address string
businessInfo.address.street          // Street address only
businessInfo.address.city            // City name
businessInfo.address.state           // State/province
businessInfo.address.zip             // Postal code

// Business identity
businessInfo.name                    // Full business name
businessInfo.shortName               // Abbreviated name
businessInfo.tagline                 // Business tagline
businessInfo.description             // Full description
businessInfo.shortDescription        // Brief description for cards

// Social media links
businessInfo.social.facebook         // Facebook URL (optional)
businessInfo.social.instagram        // Instagram URL (optional)
businessInfo.social.twitter          // Twitter URL (optional)
businessInfo.social.linkedin         // LinkedIn URL (optional)

// Business offerings
businessInfo.features               // Array of key features
businessInfo.services               // Array of services offered
```

### Business Hours Integration
```typescript
// Use the business hours function
import { getCurrentBusinessStatus } from '@data/businessInfo';

const status = getCurrentBusinessStatus();

// Display logic
{status.isOpen ? (
  <span className={styles.open}>{status.message}</span>
) : (
  <span className={styles.closed}>{status.message}</span>
)}

// Individual hours display
{Object.entries(businessInfo.hours).map(([day, hours]) => (
  <div key={day}>
    <span>{day.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + day.slice(1)}:</span>
    <span>{hours}</span>
  </div>
))}
```

### SEO Data Integration
```typescript
// Generate page-specific SEO data
import { generateSEOData } from '@data/businessInfo';

const seoData = generateSEOData('Home'); // Page title
const seoData = generateSEOData('About Us'); // About page
const seoData = generateSEOData(); // Default homepage

// Use in meta tags or head component
<title>{seoData.title}</title>
<meta name="description" content={seoData.description} />
<meta name="keywords" content={seoData.keywords} />
<meta property="og:title" content={seoData.ogTitle} />
<meta property="og:description" content={seoData.ogDescription} />
<meta property="og:url" content={seoData.ogUrl} />
<meta property="og:image" content={seoData.ogImage} />
```

### Google Maps Integration
```typescript
// Get Google Maps URL for directions
import { getGoogleMapsUrl, getDirectionsText } from '@data/businessInfo';

const mapsUrl = getGoogleMapsUrl();
const directionsText = getDirectionsText();

// Use in links
<a href={mapsUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
  {directionsText}
</a>
```

### Path Alias Usage
```typescript
// ALWAYS use path aliases for imports
import { businessInfo } from '@data/businessInfo'; // ✅ CORRECT
import { Header } from '@components/Header/Header'; // ✅ CORRECT

// NEVER use relative paths for data imports
import { businessInfo } from '../../../data/businessInfo'; // ❌ WRONG
```

## Examples

### Good Examples

#### Header Component Integration
```typescript
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { businessInfo, getCurrentBusinessStatus } from '@data/businessInfo';
import styles from './Header.module.css';

const Header: React.FC = () => {
  const businessStatus = getCurrentBusinessStatus();

  return (
    <header className={styles.header}>
      <div className={styles.headerContent}>
        <div className={styles.logo}>
          <h1 className={styles.logoText}>{businessInfo.shortName}</h1>
        </div>
        
        <div className={styles.businessStatus}>
          <span className={`${styles.statusText} ${businessStatus.isOpen ? styles.open : styles.closed}`}>
            {businessStatus.message}
          </span>
        </div>
        
        <div className={styles.directions}>
          <a 
            href={`https://maps.google.com/maps?q=${encodeURIComponent(businessInfo.address.full)}`}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            className={styles.directionsLink}
          >
            Get directions to {businessInfo.address.full}
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>
  );
};
```

#### Footer Component Integration
