### Bad Examples

#### Hardcoded Business Information
```typescript
const Header: React.FC = () => {
  return (
    <header>
      <h1>Broken Loop Brewing</h1> {/* ❌ Hardcoded business name */}
      <p>123 Main St, Anytown, USA</p> {/* ❌ Hardcoded address */}
      <a href="tel:555-123-4567">555-123-4567</a> {/* ❌ Hardcoded phone */}
    </header>
  );
};
```
*Fails: Business information is hardcoded instead of using centralized data.*

#### Relative Import Paths
```typescript
import { businessInfo } from '../../../data/businessInfo'; // ❌ Relative path
import { Header } from '../../components/Header/Header'; // ❌ Relative path
```
*Fails: Uses relative paths instead of path aliases for imports.*

#### Missing Error Handling
```typescript
const businessStatus = getCurrentBusinessStatus();
const displayName = businessInfo.name; // ❌ No fallback
```
*Fails: No error handling or fallbacks for potentially missing data.*

## Implementation Guidelines

### Updates and Maintenance Protocol
- **Business Information Changes**: Update ONLY `src/data/businessInfo.ts`
- **New Business Data**: Add to appropriate section in `businessInfo.ts`
- **Contact Updates**: Modify contact object in `businessInfo.ts`
- **Hours Changes**: Update hours object in `businessInfo.ts`
- **Address Changes**: Update address object and coordinates in `businessInfo.ts`
- **SEO Updates**: Business info changes automatically update SEO data

### Error Handling Patterns
```typescript
// Always provide fallbacks for dynamic data
const businessStatus = getCurrentBusinessStatus() || {
  isOpen: false,
  message: 'Hours not available - please contact us',
  status: 'unknown'
};

// Safe property access for optional social links
const socialLinks = Object.entries(businessInfo.social)
  .filter(([platform, url]) => url) // Only include platforms with URLs
  .map(([platform, url]) => ({ platform, url }));

// Fallback for missing business data
const displayName = businessInfo.name || businessInfo.shortName || 'Business Name';
```

### Data Types Enforcement
```typescript
// Use the exported TypeScript interfaces
import type { BusinessInfo } from '@data/businessInfo';

// Ensure type safety when extending business info
interface ExtendedBusinessInfo extends BusinessInfo {
  // Add custom business-specific fields here
  specialOffers?: string[];
  certifications?: string[];
}
```

### Business-Agnostic Design Principles
- Template must work for ANY business type
- No hardcoded industry-specific terms
- Flexible data structure accommodates different business models
- Configurable features and services arrays
- Optional social media platforms
- Adaptable business hours format
- Generic contact methods support

### Validation Requirements - BEFORE DEPLOYMENT
- [ ] All required fields in `businessInfo.ts` are populated
- [ ] Phone number format is consistent (formatted vs raw vs link)
- [ ] All social media links are valid URLs or removed
- [ ] Coordinates are accurate for map integration
- [ ] Business hours are current and correctly formatted
- [ ] Email address is valid and monitored
- [ ] Address is complete and accurate
- [ ] Website URLs are correct and functional

### Integration Checklist - MANDATORY
- [ ] Import `businessInfo` in all components using business data
- [ ] Use structured data instead of hardcoded values
- [ ] Implement proper error handling and fallbacks
- [ ] Add TypeScript interfaces for any custom data structures
- [ ] Test business hours display functionality
- [ ] Validate contact information display
- [ ] Check social media link rendering
- [ ] Verify address and directions functionality
- [ ] Test SEO data generation
- [ ] Ensure responsive design for all business info displays

